DTEND;TZID=Australia/Melbourne:20260820T131500
SUMMARY:Macroeconomics – Nic Kozeniauskas (Bank of Portugal) – Beyond R
 isk: Firm Financing and Interest Rates
LOCATION:Room 404\, FBE Building\, 111 Barry St\, Carlton VIC 3053
DESCRIPTION:Nic Kozeniauskas: “Beyond Risk: Firm Financing and Interest R
 ates”\nhttps://nicjkoz.com/\n\nZoom: https://unimelb.zoom.us/j/840556770
 57?pwd=q1KyfcUkOWfMfEThCYsc9fs2jh2vCa.1&from=addon\n\nGoogle Maps: https:/
 /maps.app.goo.gl/BirLkJKurX9pSbBB8\n\nABSTRACT:\nFirm financing is a centr
 al component of modern macroeconomic theory\, yet the empirical determinan
 ts of interest rates are not well understood. We study these using a novel
  loan-level dataset. Interest rates vary substantially across firms\, even
  on observationally equivalent loans. Default risk—the core source of di
 spersion in standard models—can only account for 15% of variation. Bank 
 heterogeneity and relationship banking have similarly limited explanatory 
 power. Instead\, most dispersion reflects persistent idiosyncratic firm-le
 vel heterogeneity—accounting for 27% of variation—that cannot be expla
 ined by observable firm characteristics. Our findings suggest that there a
 re substantial frictions in credit markets outside existing frameworks.
URL:https://unimelb.zoom.us/j/84055677057?pwd=q1KyfcUkOWfMfEThCYsc9fs2jh2vC
 a.1&from=addon
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:c026d94d1aef5379ded841733d5b83ac@generated
DTSTAMP:20260808T192131Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260808T192131Z
SEQUENCE:0
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Melbourne:20260827T120000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Melbourne:20260827T131500
SUMMARY:Macroeconomics – Maxime Gravoueille (Monash) – The Formation of
  Knowledge Spillovers and Product Market Competition: An Endogenous Networ
 k Approach (joint with Philip Uschev and Yves Zenou)
LOCATION:Room 404\, FBE Building\, 111 Barry St\, Carlton VIC 3053
DESCRIPTION:Maxime Gravoueille: “The Formation of Knowledge Spillovers an
 d Product Market Competition: An Endogenous Network Approach (joint with P
 hilip Uschev and Yves Zenou)”\nhttps://www.maximegravoueille.com/\n\nZoo
 m: https://unimelb.zoom.us/j/84055677057?pwd=q1KyfcUkOWfMfEThCYsc9fs2jh2vC
 a.1&from=addon\n\nGoogle Maps: https://maps.app.goo.gl/BirLkJKurX9pSbBB8\n
 \nABSTRACT:\nWe develop a theory of endogenous network formation in innova
 tion. Firms strategically choose positions in two coupled characteristic s
 paces — technology and product — generating networks of knowledge spil
 lovers and product market competition as equilibrium outcomes rather than 
 exogenous primitives. When networks are endogenous\, the impact of R&D pol
 icy depends not only on direct monetary incentive effects but also on the 
 equilibrium response of firms' positions\, generating welfare implications
  that differ qualitatively from those under fixed networks. We characteriz
 e how policy interventions propagate through the endogenous networks\, der
 ive optimal R&D subsidies\, and quantify the welfare gains from targeted r
 elative to uniform policy.
URL:https://unimelb.zoom.us/j/84055677057?pwd=q1KyfcUkOWfMfEThCYsc9fs2jh2vC
 a.1&from=addon
END:VEVENT
