SUMMARY:PhD Brown Bag Seminar – Eungwon Lee (University of Melbourne) –
  Mortgage Pricing with Imperfect Banking Competition
LOCATION:Room 304\, FBE Building\, 111 Barry St\, Carlton VIC 3053
DESCRIPTION:Eungwon Lee: “Mortgage Pricing with Imperfect Banking Competi
 tion”\n\nZoom: https://unimelb.zoom.us/j/81347271549?pwd=DX1wTJkLbR8CVfW
 XiaW65kUhzrKAvS.1\n\nGoogle Maps: https://maps.app.goo.gl/BirLkJKurX9pSbBB
 8\n\nABSTRACT:\nWe build a two-period model of mortgage lending under impe
 rfect competition. Households differ in income and choose whether to own o
 r rent\; homeowners borrow against housing and may default after a house-v
 alue shock. Lenders compete à la Cournot\, and house prices clear the hou
 sing market. The equilibrium mortgage rate decomposes into a funding cost\
 , an expected-payoff wedge for default and recovery\, and a market-power w
 edge. We use the model to study how lender competition affects borrowing\,
  default\, and homeownership\, and how the effects differ by income.
URL:https://unimelb.zoom.us/j/81347271549?pwd=DX1wTJkLbR8CVfWXiaW65kUhzrKAv
 S.1
END:VEVENT
