SUMMARY:PhD Brown Bag Seminar – Yobin Timilsena (University of Melbourne)
  – Spatial Transmission of Inequality through Education
LOCATION:Room 304\, FBE Building\, 111 Barry St\, Carlton VIC 3055
DESCRIPTION:Yobin Timilsena: “Spatial Transmission of Inequality through 
 Education”\n\nZoom: https://unimelb.zoom.us/j/81347271549?pwd=DX1wTJkLbR
 8CVfWXiaW65kUhzrKAvS.1\n\nGoogle Maps: https://maps.app.goo.gl/BirLkJKurX9
 pSbBB8\n\nABSTRACT:\nThis project explores how spatial differences in educ
 ation quality contribute to persistent inequality. I build a spatial overl
 apping-generations model where households make location and education deci
 sions that shape long-run outcomes. Education quality varies across space 
 and is influenced by school funding\, neighbourhood composition\, and asso
 ciated spatial spillovers. Using Australian data\, I aim to quantify the r
 ole of these factors in driving inequality in education and assess the imp
 act of policy interventions such as needs-based funding equalisation\, soc
 ial housing placement\, and housing supply reform.
URL:https://unimelb.zoom.us/j/81347271549?pwd=DX1wTJkLbR8CVfWXiaW65kUhzrKAv
 S.1
END:VEVENT
